## Question 4: Identify the Parts of a Shadowsocks URL

Given URL:

`ss://asghar:1234!!@ss.myproxy.com:1234#shadowSocks1`

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    U["ss://asghar:1234!!@ss.myproxy.com:1234#shadowSocks1"]
    U --> S["Scheme: ss"]
    U --> I["Info before @: asghar:1234!!"]
    U --> H["Host: ss.myproxy.com"]
    U --> P["Port: 1234"]
    U --> F["Fragment: shadowSocks1"]
```

| Part                   | Value            | Description                                                                    |
| ---------------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Scheme                 | `ss`             | Indicates the Shadowsocks protocol.                                            |
| Information before `@` | `asghar:1234!!`  | Contains connection or authentication information in this URL.                 |
| Host                   | `ss.myproxy.com` | The address of the server.                                                     |
| Port                   | `1234`           | The port used to connect to the server.                                        |
| Fragment               | `shadowSocks1`   | A label used to identify the connection. It is usually not sent to the server. |

> **Note:** In common `Shadowsocks` URL formats, the part before `@` usually contains encoded encryption-method and password information, rather than separate username and password fields. Therefore, interpreting `asghar` as the username and `1234!!` as the password depends on the specific URL format.

